From 5bc5f12ad8317f7ec61863ce27d078a06050113c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:12:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui: orange toasts with black text; translate the welcome page
 header

Toasts ("FlyWeb is now your default browser" and the other ToastView
toasts) were red with dark red text: Brave replaces
AddMaterialUiColorMixer() and never sets kColorToastBackgroundProminent,
so it fell back to the placeholder red. Set it to FlyWeb orange
(#FF9900) with black text and button, like the welcome page's buttons,
in light and dark mode. Same component on macOS and Linux.

IDS_WELCOME_HEADER ("Welcome to FlyWeb", the welcome tab title) had no
translation in brave_components_resources_*.xtb. Add, for all 54
languages, the existing translation of the same text (same message id)
from brave_strings_*.xtb. The rest of the welcome strings were already
translated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2hjxRPyuefYzGRoZRk
